{"abstract":"A saddlepoint of an n × n matrix is an entry that is the maximum of its row and the minimum of its column. Saddlepoints give the value of a two-player zero-sum game, corresponding to its pure-strategy Nash equilibria; efficiently finding a saddlepoint is thus a natural and fundamental algorithmic task. For finding a strict saddlepoint (an entry that is the strict maximum of its row and the strict minimum of its column) we recently gave an O(n log∗ n)-time algorithm, improving the O(n log n) bounds from 1991 of Bienstock, Chung, Fredman, Schäffer, Shor, Suri and of Byrne and Vaserstein. In this paper we present an optimal O(n)-time algorithm for finding a strict saddlepoint based on random sampling. Our algorithm, like earlier approaches, accesses matrix entries only via unit-cost binary comparisons. For finding a (non-strict) saddlepoint, we extend an existing lower bound to randomized algorithms, showing that the trivial O(n2) runtime cannot be improved even with the use of randomness.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dallant, Justin","Haagensen, Frederik","Jacob, Riko","Kozma, László","Wild, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818237"],"event":{"acronym":"ESA","title":"European Symposium on Algorithms"},"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Berlin","University Libre du Bruxelles","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Nash equilibria","Randomized algorithm","Time complexity","saddlepoint"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"an optimal randomized algorithm for finding the saddlepoint","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPICS.ESA.2024.44","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818237","identifier":[{"id":"85205695757","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-4448e628-9e81-4a2d-8f2e-7f20d7123fc1"],"keyword":["matrix-game","nash-equilibria","randomized-algorithm","saddlepoint","time-complexity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-932F2EA775045A3862A95AF7DAAF5C4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPICS.ESA.2024.44","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2401.06512","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"be","key":"university libre du bruxelles","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Libre du Bruxelles","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Programming Logic and Semantics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"free university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin","key":"dallantpau","last":"Dallant","name":"Dallant, Justin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"haagensenpau","last":"Haagensen","locid":"672280b6-17c9-4191-9b00-8f1322fc1d90","name":"Haagensen, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0002-4161-4442","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Riko","key":"jacobpau","last":"Jacob","locid":"e6f70fb0-caf1-4736-b583-b0777bc1390f","name":"Jacob, Riko","orcid":"0000-0001-9470-1809","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"László","key":"kozmapau","last":"Kozma","name":"Kozma, László","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"wildpau","last":"Wild","name":"Wild, Sebastian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.esa.2024.44","issn":["18688969"],"journal":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","pages":"1-12","publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl - Leibniz-Zentrum fuer Informatik GmbH","status":"p","title":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics","title_org":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs)","volume":"308"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85205695757"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-4448e628-9e81-4a2d-8f2e-7f20d7123fc1"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"An Optimal Randomized Algorithm for Finding the Saddlepoint.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818237","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"A saddlepoint of an n × n matrix A is an entry of A that is a maximum in its row and a minimum in its column. Knuth (1968) gave several different algorithms for finding a saddlepoint. The worst-case running time of these algorithms is Θ(n2), and Llewellyn, Tovey, and Trick (1988) showed that this cannot be improved, as in the worst case all entries of A may need to be queried. A strict saddlepoint of A is an entry that is the strict maximum in its row and the strict minimum in its column. The strict saddlepoint (if it exists) is unique, and Bienstock, Chung, Fredman, Schaffer, Shor, and Suri (1991) showed that it can be found in time O(n lg n), where a dominant runtime contribution is sorting the diagonal of the matrix. This upper bound has not been improved since 1991. In this paper we show that the strict saddlepoint can be found in O(n lg* n) ⊂ o(n lg n) time, where lg* denotes the very slowly growing iterated logarithm function, coming close to the lower bound of Ω(n). In fact, we can also compute, within the same runtime, the value of a non-strict saddlepoint, assuming one exists. Our algorithm is based on a simple recursive approach, a feasibility test inspired by searching in sorted matrices, and a relaxed notion of saddlepoint.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Jacob, Riko","Dallant, Justin","Haagensen, Frederik","Kozma, László","Wild, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759429"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Berlin","University Libre du Bruxelles","University of Liverpool"],"keyword":["Algorithm","MATRIX","saddlepoint"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"finding the saddlepoint faster than sorting","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977936.17","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759429","identifier":[{"id":"85183289736","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f66f2f78-0ae0-4f6f-ac54-202e37adb329"],"keyword":["algorithm","iterated logarithm","matrix","saddlepoint","strict saddlepoint"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-FAD5F7EE6EC9A14292E87908E4DEEAAB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1137/1.9781611977936.17","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science, Algorithms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"be","key":"university libre du bruxelles","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University Libre du Bruxelles","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"free university of berlin","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Free University of Berlin","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Riko","key":"jacobpau","last":"Jacob","locid":"e6f70fb0-caf1-4736-b583-b0777bc1390f","name":"Jacob, Riko","orcid":"0000-0001-9470-1809","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Justin","key":"dallantpau","last":"Dallant","name":"Dallant, Justin","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"haagensenpau","last":"Haagensen","locid":"672280b6-17c9-4191-9b00-8f1322fc1d90","name":"Haagensen, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0002-4161-4442","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"László","key":"kozmapau","last":"Kozma","name":"Kozma, László","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Sebastian","key":"wildpau","last":"Wild","name":"Wild, Sebastian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1137/1.9781611977936.17","eisbn":["9781611977936"],"pages":"168-178","publisher":"Society for Industrial and Applied Mathematics","status":"p","title":"2024 Symposium on Simplicity in Algorithms (SOSA)"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f66f2f78-0ae0-4f6f-ac54-202e37adb329"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Finding the saddlepoint faster than sorting","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759429","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We present a game-theoretic approach to analyzing the incentive structure in formal models of inter-organizational businesses processes. In such processes, the choices of each participants influence the outcome of others. A potential participant may be torn between the prospect of a highly preferable outcome on the one hand (e.g., a bonus on timely delivery), and the possibility that another player may make a choice (e.g., reallocation of the fast trucks) which renders that outcome impossible to achieve. We propose (a) an analysis which given the preferences of participants determines if the collaboration is at all meaningful; (b) an algorithm for modifying the incentive structure of such a process using both fines and outcome re-distribution to increase the benefit for all participants; and (c) a practical way of computing this algorithm while concealing the preferences of the collaborators for each other using secure multi-party computation.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Haagensen, Frederik","Debois, Søren"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-818232"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Game theory","Incentive design","Mechanism design","Secure Multi party Computation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incentive alignment through secure computations","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85138778674","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-818232","identifier":[{"id":"85138778674","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0931c2fc-e8d3-48d1-af65-e7433aca2b38"],"keyword":["game theory","incentive design","inter-organizational processes","mechanism design","secure multi-party computation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-32EF0DFF021C264F17D02A216EDF0A52"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Theoretical Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"haagensenpau","last":"Haagensen","locid":"672280b6-17c9-4191-9b00-8f1322fc1d90","name":"Haagensen, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0002-4161-4442","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"deboispau","last":"Debois","name":"Debois, Søren","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claudio Di Ciccio","key":"remcopedh","last":"Remco","name":"Remco, Claudio Di Ciccio","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dijkman","key":"adeladelríoortegapedh","last":"Adela del Río Ortega","name":"Adela del Río Ortega, Dijkman","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Stefanie","key":"rinderlemapedh","last":"Rinderle-Ma","name":"Rinderle-Ma, Stefanie","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-16103-2_23","edition":"1","eisbn":["9783031161032"],"isbn":["9783031161025"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"343-360","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","subtitle":"20th International Conference, BPM 2022, Münster, Germany, September 11–16, 2022, Proceedings","title":"Business Process Management","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85138778674"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0931c2fc-e8d3-48d1-af65-e7433aca2b38"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Incentive Alignment Through Secure Computations","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-818232","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"RATIONALE: Atherosclerosis can be achieved in animals by germline genetic engineering, leading to hypercholesterolemia, but such models are constrained to few species and strains, and they are difficult to combine with other powerful techniques involving genetic manipulation or variation. OBJECTIVE: To develop a method for induction of atherosclerosis without germline genetic engineering. METHODS AND RESULTS: Recombinant adeno-associated viral vectors were engineered to encode gain-of-function proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 mutants, and mice were given a single intravenous vector injection followed by high-fat diet feeding. Plasma proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 and total cholesterol increased rapidly and were maintained at high levels, and after 12 weeks, mice had atherosclerotic lesions in the aorta. Histology of the aortic root showed progression of lesions to the fibroatheromatous stage. To demonstrate the applicability of this method for rapid analysis of the atherosclerosis susceptibility of a mouse strain and for providing temporal control over disease induction, we demonstrated the accelerated atherosclerosis of mature diabetic Akita mice. Furthermore, the versatility of this approach for creating atherosclerosis models also in nonmurine species was demonstrated by inducing hypercholesterolemia and early atherosclerosis in Golden Syrian hamsters. CONCLUSIONS: Single injections of proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9-encoding recombinant adeno-associated viral vectors are a rapid and versatile method to induce atherosclerosis in animals. This method should prove useful for experiments that are high-throughput or involve genetic techniques, strains, or species that do not combine well with current genetically engineered models.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bjørklund, Martin Mæng","Hollensen, Anne Kruse","Hagensen, Mette K","Dagnæs-Hansen, Frederik","Christoffersen, Christina","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S02-095.82-029648"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"induction of atherosclerosis in mice and hamsters without germline genetic engineering","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCRESAHA.114.302937","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.82-029648","identifier":[{"id":"24677271","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84901449412","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-ea36ecd1-e066-4e66-81ab-cd2823b85980","ku-a7c95c74-05c4-44dc-a37d-3f92fb86faad"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-98521FEC5D84ABD1D0CD11317E31DFFF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/CIRCRESAHA.114.302937","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Hjertemedicinsk Afdeling B, SKS"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"a